     "result_text_tail": "un-rate operating income to roughly $26M, above the lender's $20M requirement. The deck also compares five options (including management's draft and exiting home delivery), shows the calculations, and closes with risks, stage gates and six board decisions.\n\n**Hypotheses:** I started from the view that fixing promotions and e-commerce alone would be enough. Tested against the pack, that reaches only about 2.1%, so I added the labor rebalance and store exits. The deck shows this on slide 3.\n\nChoices I made in place of asking you (all listed in the appendix):\n- **Timing:** I read FY2025 as ending January 2026, so FY2026, the year the $20M covenant applies to, closes as the board meets. The pack has no FY2026 results, so I used FY2025 as the run-rate.\n- **Wage rise:** half of the 2027 increase is assumed to be recovered through prices.\n- **Vendor funding:** the pack doesn't say how markdowns are recorded, so this figure is indicative and is set to zero in the low case.\n- **Weak stores:** the pack only gives totals for the nine, so I split them pro rata by store count.\n- **One-time costs:** apart from the $7.5M lease-exit figure from the pack, these are my planning allowances.\n\nThe sandbox blocked me from opening the deck in PowerPoint. I checked the layout with my own previews, which is also how the PDF was made, so it is a close but not exact copy of the PowerPoint rendering.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- Harlow_margin_plan_board_Feb2027.pptx\n- Harlow_margin_plan_preview.pdf"
    }
